		{"id":"f9b5f794d27bab5b","x":-125,"y":-680,"width":725,"height":1660,"type":"text","text":"# ⭐ **GEOMETRY (the part most people miss)**\n\nMoment Canvas Types are arranged **radially** around a central core.\n\nCode\n\n```\n                 [ MOMENT CORE ]\n                        |\n   -------------------------------------------------\n   |       |         |         |         |        |\n Static  Dynamic  Tension  Resonance  Navigation  Choice\n   |       |         |         |         |        |\n                Encounter       Threshold\n```\n\nThis radial layout matters because:\n\n- Types can **rotate** into each other\n    \n- Types can **collapse** into Tension\n    \n- Types can **expand** into Resonance\n    \n- Types can **shift** into Navigation\n    \n- Types can **invert** into Threshold\n    \n\nIt’s a **taxonomy**, but it’s also a **map**.\n\n# ⭐ **HOW TYPES INTERACT WITH THE FLOW**\n\nThis is the part that makes your system _sing_:\n\n- **Flow = how a moment moves**\n    \n- **Types = what shape the moment is before it moves**\n    \n\nFlow is the choreography. Types are the geometry.\n\nFlow is the dance. Types are the stage.\n\nFlow is the physics. Types are the topology.\n\n# ⭐ **THE CLEAN ASCII VERSION (ready for your vault)**\n\nCode\n\n```\n                 ┌──────────────────────┐\n                 │     MOMENT CORE      │\n                 └──────────────────────┘\n                          /|\\\n                           |\n        -------------------------------------------------\n        |        |         |         |         |        |\n   [Static]  [Dynamic]  [Tension]  [Resonance] [Navigation]\n        |        |         |         |         |        \n                        [Choice]\n                           |\n                      [Encounter]\n                           |\n                      [Threshold]\n```"}
